# PC1 of capital forms, Younger Bronze Age (1100-500 BCE)

PCA, correlation basis, 39 slices (4300-500 BCE), 12 Z variables. Sign anchored so ZCU_AU (largest |loading|, +0.407) is positive.
Variance explained: PC1 30.33%, PC2 19.47% (49.79% together).

| BCE | PC1 | delta vs 1100 | z vs 1000-500 (n=6; mean 1.412, sd 0.571) | outside +/-2 SD |
|-----|-------|---------|-------|------|
|1100 | 4.447 | -       | +5.31 | YES |
|1000 | 2.148 | -2.299  | +1.29 | no |
| 900 | 1.627 | -2.820  | +0.38 | no |
| 800 | 1.894 | -2.553  | +0.84 | no |
| 700 | 1.225 | -3.222  | -0.33 | no |
| 600 | 0.800 | -3.648  | -1.07 | no |
| 500 | 0.779 | -3.669  | -1.11 | no |

PC1(1100) is the maximum of the whole 39-slice series; jump 1100->1000 = -2.299; 79.5% of PC1 variance within YBA
comes from the 1100 slice alone (var 1.588 -> 0.326).

Robustness (sign aligned to main PC1, r = 0.953-0.983; 1100 stays rank 1/7 in every variant):
- without ZHort: PC1(1100) 3.518, delta +2.592, z +10.56
- without ZCU_AU: PC1(1100) 3.521, delta +1.712, z +2.87
- without ZHort+ZCU_AU: PC1(1100) 2.365, delta +1.003, z +23.34 (sd of the rest collapses to 0.043 -> use delta/rank)
- YBA-only PCA (excl. ZSichel, ZKeform zero variance): PC1(1100) 5.349 vs mean -0.892 (sd 0.909), z +6.86, EVR PC1 62.5%
- no PCA at all (mean of raw Z): 1100 = 0.727, z +5.31; excluding ZHort+ZCU_AU 0.249, z +9.61

Drivers of the +3.03 gap (loading x Z-gap, sums to 3.025): ZCU_AU +1.169, ZHort +0.789, Zhausgr +0.459,
ZDolch +0.420, ZMonument +0.381, Zkeverz -0.214, others ~0.

Pollen (Belau_PC1_inter 100-yr means, qualitative only): 1100 = 0.654, 1000 = 2.676, 900 = 2.307, 800 = 5.455;
record ends at 702 BCE, so 700/600/500 BCE have zero coverage and no claim is made for them.

Limitations: n = 6 in the comparison window (z reported descriptively, not as a significance test); many Z values are
interpolated/plateaued within the YBA, which may inflate the uniqueness of the 1100 slice.
